 course as you see him in the middle  there to the right of elena we have  bucky the winner soldier and it's going  to be interesting to see him fight  alongside with this team especially us  agent john walker if you're unfamiliar  with who the thunderbolts team is it's  essentially a group of not so much  villains even though villains are a big  part of the team but kind of a group of  misfit heroes all of which who have  committed crimes before now they are  working for the government doing  assignments for the government to  essentially stay out of jail it's kind  of their second chance it's basically  the suicide squad and this was probably  the biggest reveal for d23 although  there are some other big ones we're  about to talk about this was probably  the big one now they did talk about  ant-man and the wasp quantum mania they  showed footage for it but it was the  same footage that was shown at sdcc i  did a breakdown of that you can find it  on my channel they did however show a  little bit more of king and apparently  he is absolutely terrifying and jonathan  majors absolutely crushed it with that  role we also saw a little bit more of a  glimpse of kang with the loki season 2  teaser again that was only showed to the  people who were there but what we saw  was loki traveling through different  points in time he was actually being  pulled through different points in time  loki says that he has seen terrible  awful things he also looks at a wall  covered in kang decorations and he says  war is on its way they also did confirm  that ki hoi kwon is going to be joining  the cast and is a tva employee of course  owen wilson was there as well and i'll  do a full breakdown on what we saw on  this loki season 2 trailer later on as  well now for those of you who have been  watching she-hulk and have been talking  about the leader the leader is confirmed  to be returning to the mcu in captain  america new world order returning from  the incredible hulk tim blake nelson is  coming back to the mcu as the leader and  apparently rumor has it so take it with  a big grain of salt because a lot of  rumors were wrong about d23 but  apparently rumor has it that there's  going to be a lot of hulk stuff in  captain america 4 which makes sense  given the connection to the leader the  super soldier serum and of course bruce  banner hopefully this leads up to a solo  hulk film which unfortunately we did not  get an announcement for today now armor  wars got a new logo but that's about it  they did reveal that secret invasion is  going to lead right into armor wars and  roadie seems to be playing a significant  part in secret invasion as well now i  think the second biggest reveal that we  kind of already knew was for ekko and  daredevil they announced the main  villain of the echo series is of course  kingpin they showed footage for ekko and  kingpin was in the very last shot with a  bandage over his eye where ekko shot him  at the end of the hawkeye series as the  cast of the echo series got off the  stage vincent d'onofrio actually stayed  on stage and then charlie cox came out  confirming kingpin is the villain of  daredevil born again as well they then  showed us some she-hulk footage of  she-hulk and daredevil interacting with  each other which we'll see pretty soon  in she-hulk and the last thing that they  talked about and showed us was for the  marvels and they gave a little sneak  peek of that as well just to the people  watching we see nick fury talking to  captain monica rambo as she's wearing an  astronaut suit in space she touches  something in space and swaps spots with  kamala khan in which rambo tells kamala  khan our light-based powers are  entangled which could explain what  happened at the end of miss marvel  captain marvel and kamala khan switched  places and it could be because of this  reason right here and that was marvel's  d23 panel what they did give us was  pretty exciting unfortunately we didn't  really get anything about the fantastic  four nothing about deadpool 3 and  nothing about the mutants which i didn't  really think we'd hear about anyways and  despite these cool reveals and the  really cool trailers and sneak peeks  that we got i know a lot of people  including myself are going to be  disappointed that they didn't reveal  anything about phase six we do have  disney's investors day coming up at the  end of the year but i'm not holding my  breath for that it may be marvel  studios's plan to wait till the next  sdcc of 2023 to reveal the entirety of  phase six hopefully we don't have to  wait that long but as we can see from  d23 there is a lot to keep us occupied  in the meantime a lot of really cool  things happening really soon in the  marvel cinematic universe so if you want  to stay up to date on all the latest  news be sure to subscribe and hit that  notification bell so you don't miss any  videos don't forget to like the video  and for live updates you can follow me  on instagram or twitter as always thank  you all so much for watching woof  you

